# ZGC tuning profile — RecSys backend service
#
# When to choose ZGC:
#   Sub-10 ms pause requirement (latency-critical inference path),
#   heap ≥ 1 GB, Java 21+ (Generational ZGC — significantly better throughput
#   than classic ZGC). Tradeoff: higher CPU overhead vs. G1 (~10–20% more CPU
#   for concurrent GC threads); not ideal for CPU-bound batch workloads.
#
# ZGC STW pause anatomy (all < 1 ms in practice):
#   Initial mark   — scan GC roots; STW ≈ 0.1 ms
#   Final mark     — rescan roots mutated during concurrent mark; STW ≈ 0.5 ms
#   Relocate start — select relocation set; STW ≈ 0.1 ms
#   Remaining work (mark, remap, relocate) runs fully concurrent.
#
# CMS note: CMS is deprecated (Java 9) and removed (Java 14). If you are on an
#   older JVM, replace -XX:+UseZGC with -XX:+UseConcMarkSweepGC and add
#   -XX:CMSInitiatingOccupancyFraction=70 -XX:+UseCMSInitiatingOccupancyOnly.
#   Migrate to ZGC or G1 at the earliest opportunity — CMS has no fragmentation
#   defense and degrades to Serial Full GC under promotion failure.
#
# Usage:
#   java $(cat jvm-zgc.options) -jar recsys-api-*.jar    (Java 21+)

# ── Heap ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ZGC requires more headroom than G1 because concurrent relocation needs free
# space for copying while the mutator runs. Rule of thumb: leave 25–50% spare.
-Xms1g
-Xmx4g

# ── ZGC collector (Java 21 Generational ZGC) ─────────────────────────────────
-XX:+UseZGC
# Generational ZGC (Java 21+): separate young/old regions dramatically reduce
# the amount of heap scanned per cycle, cutting CPU overhead by ~50% vs classic ZGC.
-XX:+ZGenerational

# Proactive GC: start a new cycle every 5 s even when heap pressure is low.
# Prevents large spikes when traffic bursts arrive on a full old gen.
-XX:ZCollectionInterval=5

# Return unused heap pages to the OS after 5 minutes of disuse.
# Reduces RSS footprint between traffic peaks without forcing a GC.
-XX:ZUncommitDelay=300

# Number of concurrent GC threads. Default = ncpu/4 (often too few for bursty
# workloads). Increase if /health/gc shows allocationStalls > 0.
# -XX:ConcGCThreads=4   # uncomment and tune to your vCPU count

# ── Stack ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-Xss256k

# ── Metaspace ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-XX:MetaspaceSize=128m
-XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=256m

# ── GC logging — ZGC cycle / STW pauses / safepoints ─────────────────────────
# gc*        : all ZGC phases (concurrent mark, relocate, remap, STW pauses)
# safepoint  : non-GC STW events (e.g. class redefinition, deoptimization)
-Xlog:gc*,safepoint=info:file=gc-zgc.log:time,uptime,level:filecount=5,filesize=20m

# ── Diagnostics ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:HeapDumpPath=heap-dump-zgc.hprof
-XX:+PrintFlagsFinal
